      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-11-28_WidnesExaminer_art0165" n="art0165">
        <head>TEAMS FOR TO-DAY.</head>
        <p>TEAMS FOR TO-DAY.</p>
        <p>PADGATE UNITED v. CADISHEAD WESLEYANS.</p>
        <p>At Padgate, where the -I;CMie team have not yet tasted defeat this season : Padgate : E. Unsworth ; Unsworth and Potter; Woods, Gilbert and Williams; Yates, Rankin- son, Ball, Higginson and Hardman (captain). Reserves: Pass and Ricketts. ELMWOOD AVENUE v. EMMANUEL INSTITUTE.</p>
        <p>'ln Victoria Park : Elmwood Avenue: Jas. Phcenix; Jos. Phcenix and W. Hall; Jos. Pritchard, E. B. Mellor and W. Finch; W. Phoenix, Jos. Smith, Ed. Ken- drick, T. Wells and W. Finch. Emmanuel: O. Bailey; E. Crozier and S. Hughes; T. Hughes, S. Banner and W. Ayres; Walter 'Eaton, A. Oakes, S. Roberts (captain), A. Bevan and William Eaton.</p>
        <p>ELM WOOD AVENUE IL V. C.L.C. Elmwood Avenue IL: R. Wallington; H. Hazeldine and Jas. Mellor; H. L. Clayton, F. Rowland and T. Dutton; P. Podmore, T. Hunt, W. Farrar, W. Littlewood and R. Kendrick.</p>
        <p>GREAT SANKEY v. CALDER AND MERSEY. At Penketh, in • the Widnes and District Alliance; kick-off 2.45:— Great Sankey: H. Brindle; E. Glover and B. J. Kelly; J. E. Glover, H. Ditchfield and H. Payne; T. Roberts, T. Whitfield, T: Hawthorn, S. Poulter and A. Houghton.</p>
