        <p>BOARD OF TRADE.—SESSION 1915. WARRINGTON CORPORATION ELEC- TRIC LIGHTING (EXTENSION). (The supply of electricity by the Corporation of War- rington in certain parishes or townships in the rural districts of Runcorn and Warrington and the extension of the powers of the Corporation to and over those parishes; purchase of land; com- pulsory area; the repeal or amendment of the Runcorn Urban and Runcorn Rural Electric Lighting Order, 1910, and the incorporation and amendment of other Acts or Orders. NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the Mayor. Aldermen r:_nd Burgesses of the County Borough of Warrington (herein referred to as the Corporation), and whose address is the Town Hall, arrington,intend to apply to the Board of Trade 1 on or before the 21st day of December next for a Provisional Order (herein referred to as the Order) under the Electric Lighting Acts, 1882 to 1909, for all or some of the following purposes (that is to saY) 1. To extend the area of supply of the Corpora- tion under the Warrington Electric Lighting Order, 1898 (confirmed by the Electric Lighting Orders Confirmation (No. 11) Act, 1898), so as to include therein the following parishes or townships, namely: Stockton Heath, Latchford Without, Thelwall, Grappenhall, Lower Walton, Higher Walton and Appleton, all in the rural district of Runcorn in the County of Chester; and Penketh and Great Sankey. in the rural dis- trict of Warrington, in the County Palatine of Lancaster; and to authorise the Corporation to supply, distri- bute and sell electrical energy for public and private purposes within the parishes or townships above- named (herein referred to as the extended area of supply). 2. To extend and make applicable to the extended area of supply all or some of the provisions con- tained in the Warrington Electric Lighting Order, 1898, and the Warrington Corporation Act, 1911, and to apply such provisions to the undertaking to be authorised by the Order, subject to such varia- tions and exceptions as may be contained therein. 3. To incorporate some or all of the provisions contained in the Schedule to the Electric Lighting (Clauses) Act, 1899, with such modifications and exceptions as may be indicated in the Order. 4. To confer upon the Corporation all or some of the powers of the Electric Lighting Acts, 1882 to 1909, and the enactments incorporated therewith, and to alter, vary, or extinguish all rights and privileges which would or might interfere with any of the objects of the Order, and to confer all other rights and privileges necessary for carrying such olatets i•ito effect. 5. To empower the Corporation to supply elec- trical energy for purposes incidental to the working of any railway, tramway, river or canal situate partly within and partly without the extended area of supply. 6. To alter, extend, repeal or amend the provi- sions of the Warrington Electric Lighting Order, 1898, the Warrington Corporation Act. 1911, and the Runcorn Urban and Runcorn Rural Electric Light- ing Order, 1910, and the Acts confirming the same. 7. The streets in which it is proposed that elec- tric lines shall be laid down in the extended area of supply within a specified time are as follows: In the rural district of Runcorn: Old London-road from the borough boundary to the Police Station, Stockton Heath. In the rural district of 'Warrington: Liverpool-road from the borough boundary to the western boundary of the Sankey Wire Mills. S. The following are the streets not repairable by the local authority and railways which the Corpora 4 tion propose to take powers to break up:— Borough of Warrington: Greenbank-street and the culvert belonging to the Manchester Ship Canal Company under the said Canal and the approaches thereto. Parish of Walton Superior: Walton Bridge and approaches carrying Hatton and Walton-road over the Bridgewater Canal; Hough's Bridge and approaches carrying Rough's-lane over the Bridgewater Canal. Parish of Stockton Heath: Stockton Bridge and approaches carrying the Northwich-road over the Bridgewater Canal; Red-lane Bridge and approaches carrying Red-lane over the Bridge- water Canal. • Parish of Thelwall: Shepherd's-bank Bridges and approaches carrying the Warrington-road , over the London and North-Western Railway ' (Warrington and Stockport branch) and over the old railway siding. Parish of Grappenhall: Bridge and approaches carrying Bellhouse-lane over the Bridgewater Canal. 9. To confer upon the Corporation all or some of the powers of the Lands Clauses Act, 1845, to take land otherwise than by agreement for the purpose of a generating or transformer station in respect of all that piece or parcel of land situate on the south side of West Avenue, in the parish of Stock- ton Heath in the County of Chester, adjoining the passage on the west side of the cycle shop in the occupation of the Royal Alfred Cycle Company, containing by admeasurement 343 square yards or thereabouts, and now in the occupation of Joseph Taylor and Jonathan William Welsby, which lands are more particularly delineated, coloured and described upon a plan and book of reference de- posited at the offices of the Corporation: and in connection therewith to lay a main or mains along Wilderspool-causeway, Greenbank-street, through the north bank of the Manchester Ship Canal, under the said canal by the existing culvert, across Elles- mere-road, and along Old London-road to the trans- former station before mentioned in West-avenue. AND NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the raft of the Order will be deposited At the Office of the Board of Tritt4.s on or tiZfOre the Thit day of December next, and printed copies of the draft Order when deposited and of the Order when made may be obtained at the price of one shilling for each cony from the Sub-Postmaster. Great Sankey, and the Sub-Postmaster, Stockton Heath, and from the Town Clerk of Warrington and the Parliamen- tary Agents, whose names are subscribed hereto. AND NOTICE IS HEREBY FURTHER GIVEN that a map showing the boundaries of the proposed extended area of supply. and the streets in which it is proposed that electric lines shall be laid down within a specified time and a plan of the land pro- posed to be taken, with a book of reference thereto and a copy of this advertisement as published in the " London Gazette." will be deposited on or before the 30th day of November, 1914, for public inspection as follows:— With the Clerk of the Peace for the County Palatine of Lancaster at his office at Preston; with the Clerk of the Peace for the County of Chester at his office at Chester; with the Clerks to the Rural District Councils of Runcorn and Warrington respectively at their respective offices at Runcorn and Warrington: and with the Town Clerk of War- . rington at the Town Hall, Warrington. • AND NOTICE IS FURTHER GIVEN that every Local or other Authority, Company, or person de- sirous of bringing before the Board of Trade any objection respecting the application must do so by letter addressed to the Board of Trade marked on the outside of the cover enclosing it " Electric Lighting Acts " on or before the 15th day of January, 1915. and a copy of such objection must also be forwarded to the Town Clerk of Warrington or the Parlia- mentary Agents whose names are subscribed hereto. Dated this 12th November, 1914. J. LYON WHITTLE, Town Clerk, Warrington. BAKER &amp; SONS, 35, Parliament-street, Westminster, Parliamentary Agents.</p>
