        <p>LEATHER IS DEARER! Owing to the enormous quantity of Boots required for the Armies of the Allies, practically all of which have to be made in England, there is no possible doubt that Boots are certain to be MUCH DEARER. The Manufacturers demand an increase of 10 per cent. to 20 per cent., and, in certain kinds of Boots,- up to even 30 per cent. Since the outbreak of War the price of LEATHER has risen by nearly one-half. It is evident that the Public will have •to pay largely-increased prices, or accept an inferior article—one or the other. WE ARE, HOWEVER, IN THE FORTUNATE POSITION TO BE ABLE TO OFFER LARGE STOCKS OF BOOTS, SHOES AND SLIPPERS AT PRICES RULING BEFORE THE WAR. We strongly advise our friends to take advantage of these Stocks, which represent the best possible value. R. ROBERTS &amp;SON 19, BRIDGE STREET.</p>
        <p>Notices of births, marriages, and deaths, in memoriam notices, and acknowledgments of sympathy are inserted in "The Examiner" at the following rates :—Not exceeding 20 words, Is. 6d. each; every additional seven words, 6d.</p>
        <p>Marriages. CRAIK—BARKER.—November 21st, at the Parish Church, by the Rector, John, eldest son of Coun- cillor and Mrs. Craik, Greenbank, Manchester- road, to Annie, only daughter of Mr. W. S. and Mrs. Barker, Willis-street, Warrington. WHEELER BROWNE. At the Grappenhall Parish Church, on the rd November, 1914, by the Rev. Harry V. Pigot, M.A. the Rector, Oliver, third son of the late Rev. john Commins Wheeler, Vicar of Birkdale, and Dorothy. only daughter of Mr. and Mrs. Arthur Browne, "Oak- yule," Latchford Without, Warrington. WARBURTON—SMITEL—On the 24th inst., at Cairo-street Unitarian Church, by the Rev. Irvine Lister, Ernest Leopold, second son of Mr. J. P. Warburton, Latchford, to Edith Alice. youngest daughter of Mr. and Mrs. J. T. Smith, of 68, Bewsey-street.</p>
        <p>Deaths. MESSITER.—On the 23rd inst., at 27. Rolleston- street, George Malem Messiter, aged 60 years. Funeral this day at 2 p.m. RILEY.—On the 20th inst., at 9, Paul-street, John Riley, aged 47 years. HEWlTT.—November 19th; at 44, Napier-street, Thomas Hewitt, aged 75 years. ELWELL.—November 23rd, at 2, Owen-street, Bliza Elwell, aged 55 years. WlLLS.—November 23rd, at 67, New-road, Robert Wills. aged 69 years. SEFTON.—November 24th, at 54, Longford-street, George Sefton, aged 79 years. In Memoriam. MASON.—In affectionate remembrance of Harry .Mason, who died November 25th, 1910. FATHER, MOTHER and SISTERS.</p>
